---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SitePage from '../../components/SitePage.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Musings"
	description="Articles and notes by Amanda Christianson — product, systems, and the web."
>
	<SitePage
		title="Musings"
		lede="Longer writing: what I’m thinking about in product, engineering, and the craft of building for people."
	>
		<div class="font-body text-ink-muted">
			<p class="text-base leading-relaxed">
				Individual posts will live at paths like <span class="text-ink">/musings/your-post-slug</span> once
				you wire up Markdown or a CMS. For now, this index is ready for a list of articles.
			</p>

			<hr class="my-10 border-ink/10" />

			<h2 class="font-headline text-[clamp(1.75rem,4.5vw,3.5rem)] font-normal tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">
				Articles
			</h2>
			<ul class="mt-6 list-none space-y-6 p-0" aria-label="Blog posts">
				<li class="border-b border-ink/10 pb-6 last:border-b-0">
					<p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-faint">
						Coming soon
					</p>
					<p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
						Add your first post as a Markdown file or collection entry—this row will become a linked title and
						date.
					</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</SitePage>
</Layout>
